      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Simmer the bacon"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Put {{gammon-joint}} of gammon in a large pot. Cover with cold water and bring to the boil. Drain and discard the water (this removes excess salt). Cover again with fresh cold water."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add {{onion}} halved onion, {{bay-leaves}} bay leaves, and a small handful of peppercorns. Bring to a gentle simmer. Cook for 25 minutes per 500 g, so for {{gammon-joint}} of gammon, about 75 minutes total."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "About 20 minutes before the bacon is done, add {{carrot}} halved carrots to the pot. With 10 minutes left, add {{cabbage-white}} quartered cabbage."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Lift the bacon from the pot and rest for 10 minutes. Reserve 250 ml of the cooking liquid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the parsley sauce"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Melt {{unsalted-butter}} of butter in a small saucepan. Add {{plain-flour}} of flour and stir for 1 minute. Gradually whisk in {{whole-milk}} of milk and 200 ml of the reserved cooking liquid. Cook for 3 to 4 minutes until thick. Stir in {{parsley-flat}} of chopped parsley."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Serve"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slice the bacon thickly. Arrange on warm plates with the drained cabbage and carrots. Pour the parsley sauce over or alongside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "rows": [
            {
              "symptom": "Bacon is very salty",
              "cause": "Not soaked, or first water not discarded",
              "fix": "Soak the joint overnight in cold water and always discard the first cooking water. The residual salt in the meat flavours the second cooking liquid."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Cabbage is grey and mushy",
              "cause": "Added too early in the cooking",
              "fix": "Add the cabbage only in the last 10 minutes. It should be tender but still green."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Sauce is lumpy",
              "cause": "Flour paste not smooth before adding liquid",
              "fix": "Cook the butter and flour together until smooth before adding any liquid, then add the liquid gradually."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Bacon joint is still tough after the full cooking time",
              "cause": "A very thick joint, or temperature too low",
              "fix": "A rolling simmer, not a bare tremble, is needed. Continue simmering and check every 15 minutes."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Boiled bacon and cabbage is the traditional Sunday dinner of Irish cooking. It has been made across the country since at least the eighteenth century. It is sometimes confused with corned beef and cabbage, which is the Irish-American version. Irish immigrants in America used beef when they could not afford pork. The original dish uses pork: a salted joint simmered until the fat is soft. The parsley sauce is the standard accompaniment."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
